Neon containers port (M1b): no platform single sign-on in container tabs.

Platform SSO (Cloud AP on Windows, Extensible Enterprise SSO on macOS) attaches
the device account's identity to navigations of a regular profile. Container
tabs share that profile, so without this every container would be signed in
to the device's work account. Ported from brave-core v1.100.58 (bd6d26d1):
rewrite/chrome/browser/enterprise/platform_auth/platform_auth_navigation_throttle.cc.yaml
and browser/enterprise/platform_auth_helper.cc. The helper moves into the
containers component so the enterprise target needs no chrome/browser
dependency. The hook only compiles on Windows, macOS and Android, and is
unverified at runtime.

